  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The Dolby Theatre, located at Ovation Hollywood on Hollywood Boulevard and Highland Avenue in Los Angeles, is the permanent home of the Academy Awards. Opened in 2001 (formerly Kodak Theatre), the 3,400-seat venue hosts the annual Oscars ceremony, featuring state-of-the-art Dolby Vision and Dolby Atmos technology. Key Details About the Oscar Theater: Location: 6801 Hollywood Blvd, Hollywood, CA 90028. Oscar History: It has hosted the Academy Awards since 2001 and is set to remain the venue through 2028. Features: It features a 180,000-square-foot, 3,400-seat design, specifically optimized for world-class film premieres and live performances. Design & Technology: The theater includes top-tier sound, lighting, and stage technology, along with a massive stage that undergoes a transformation for the Oscars. Surrounding Area: It is located in the Ovation Hollywood shopping center (formerly Hollywood and Highland), adjacent to the iconic TCL Chinese Theatre. Other Academy Venues:The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences also uses other venues for events: Samuel Goldwyn Theater: Located in Beverly Hills. Linwood Dunn Theater: Located at the Pickford Center for Motion Picture Study in Hollywood. David Geffen/Ted Mann Theaters: Located at the Academy Museum of Motion Pictures.",
